# 32. Investigating a Successful Login

To investigate successful logons:

```text
Event Viewer
    ↓
Windows Logs
    ↓
Security
    ↓
Filter Current Log
    ↓
Event ID 4624
```

Useful fields inside the event can include:

### Account Name

The account associated with the logon.

### Logged

The time of the event.

### Source Network Address

The network address associated with the logon, when available.

### Logon Type

Provides information about the type of logon.

---

# 33. Investigating Account Creation

Question:

> Which user account was recently created?

Workflow:

```text
Security Log
     ↓
Event ID 4720
     ↓
Find relevant/latest event
     ↓
Inspect New Account
     ↓
Account Name
```

### Key Point

```text
4720 = Account Creation
```

---

# 34. Investigating Password Reset Activity

Question:

> Was an account involved in a password reset attempt?

Check:

```text
Security Log
     ↓
Event ID 4724
     ↓
Inspect Target / Account Information
```

### Key Point

```text
4724 = Attempt to Reset an Account Password
```

When investigating, make sure the account in the event matches the account being investigated.

